279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 213 0 R
/T (Modern vehicles have generally increased in size over time, while parking dimensions have only changed marginally. This has led to recurring discussions about narrow parking areas, limited space for door opening and parking damage. )
/E (Modern vehicles have generally increased in size over time, while parking dimensions have only changed marginally. This has led to recurring discussions about narrow parking areas, limited space for door opening and parking damage. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 213 0 R
/T (The purpose of the study was to investigate how existing parking garages relate to today's changed vehicle dimensions and how the parking design can be developed to improve usability and function. The study was based on literature studies, vehicle data, site studies, interviews, user tests and modelling of larger parking dimensions in existing parking garages.)
/E (The purpose of the study was to investigate how existing parking garages relate to today's changed vehicle dimensions and how the parking design can be developed to improve usability and function. The study was based on literature studies, vehicle data, site studies, interviews, user tests and modelling of larger parking dimensions in existing parking garages.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 213 0 R
/T (The results indicate that modern vehicles occupy a larger part of the parking space than previous vehicle generations, which can reduce the available space for entry and exit. Observations, interviews and user tests also indicate that users in certain situations adapt their parking behaviour to create more doorway space.)
/E (The results indicate that modern vehicles occupy a larger part of the parking space than previous vehicle generations, which can reduce the available space for entry and exit. Observations, interviews and user tests also indicate that users in certain situations adapt their parking behaviour to create more doorway space.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 213 0 R
/T (The modelling experiments indicate that the possibilities of introducing larger parking spaces can improve usability by creating more space for entry and exit. At the same time, the results indicate that the possibilities of introducing larger parking spaces in existing parking garages are often limited by garage design, column placements and available manoeuvring space. In the garages studied, larger parking spaces also resulted in a reduced parking capacity.)
/E (The modelling experiments indicate that the possibilities of introducing larger parking spaces can improve usability by creating more space for entry and exit. At the same time, the results indicate that the possibilities of introducing larger parking spaces in existing parking garages are often limited by garage design, column placements and available manoeuvring space. In the garages studied, larger parking spaces also resulted in a reduced parking capacity.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 213 0 R
/T (The study provides a basis for further discussion on how parking garages can be designed with regard to vehicle development and user needs. However, the results should be interpreted with some caution as the study is based on a limited number of case studies, interviews and user tests and therefore mainly provides exploratory indications rather than generally valid conclusions.)
/E (The study provides a basis for further discussion on how parking garages can be designed with regard to vehicle development and user needs. However, the results should be interpreted with some caution as the study is based on a limited number of case studies, interviews and user tests and therefore mainly provides exploratory indications rather than generally valid conclusions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
